1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,506
In this walkthrough, we will open FEAT
inside Neurodesk and build a map of its

2
00:00:07,506 --> 00:00:10,508
interface before changing any analysis
settings.

3
00:00:10,508 --> 00:00:15,512
FEAT is both a model-configuration
interface and a pipeline runner.

4
00:00:15,512 --> 00:00:20,516
The choices made here determine the data,
preprocessing, registration, statistical

5
00:00:20,516 --> 00:00:24,519
model, and reporting steps that FSL will
execute.

6
00:00:24,519 --> 00:00:27,021
Begin on the Neurodesktop workspace.

7
00:00:27,021 --> 00:00:32,025
Open the Applications menu, choose
Neurodesk, then Functional Imaging, FSL,

8
00:00:32,025 --> 00:00:34,527
and the approved FSL version.

9
00:00:34,527 --> 00:00:40,031
This versioned launcher prepares the
environment so the FSL commands and

10
00:00:40,031 --> 00:00:44,534
graphical tools are available in the
terminal it opens.

11
00:00:44,534 --> 00:00:50,539
That is more reproducible than assuming
that a terminal outside this environment

12
00:00:50,539 --> 00:00:53,541
is using the intended FSL installation.

13
00:00:56,333 --> 00:01:02,093
At the prompt, enter `Feat`, with a
capital F, followed by an ampersand.

14
00:01:02,093 --> 00:01:06,966
The capitalised command starts the FEAT
graphical interface; the lower-case `feat`

15
00:01:06,966 --> 00:01:09,624
command expects a saved design file.

16
00:01:09,624 --> 00:01:14,940
The ampersand returns control of the
terminal while the interface remains open.

17
00:01:14,940 --> 00:01:18,927
If the window takes a moment to appear,
wait.

18
00:01:18,927 --> 00:01:24,244
Starting another copy simply because the
launch is quiet can leave several

19
00:01:24,244 --> 00:01:26,016
indistinguishable FEAT windows open.

20
00:01:26,016 --> 00:01:32,218
FEAT may remember settings from an earlier
session, so treat every value as something

21
00:01:32,218 --> 00:01:33,104
to verify.

22
00:01:33,104 --> 00:01:38,420
A familiar-looking interface is not
evidence that the current design is safe.

23
00:01:40,433 --> 00:01:44,388
At the top of FEAT, select First-level
analysis.

24
00:01:44,388 --> 00:01:48,342
First level means one run from one
participant.

25
00:01:48,342 --> 00:01:55,262
It is not a within-subject combination
across runs, and it is not a group

26
00:01:55,262 --> 00:01:55,756
analysis.

27
00:01:55,756 --> 00:02:00,205
Keeping that unit explicit prevents
participant-specific results from being

28
00:02:00,205 --> 00:02:02,182
described as population conclusions.

29
00:02:02,182 --> 00:02:05,642
Next, select Full analysis for this
orientation.

30
00:02:05,642 --> 00:02:11,573
Full analysis exposes the steps used to
prepare and model a run.

31
00:02:11,573 --> 00:02:16,021
This is a scope choice, not a universal
recommendation.

32
00:02:16,021 --> 00:02:21,459
If the input has already been
preprocessed, the workflow must be

33
00:02:21,459 --> 00:02:26,401
adjusted so that motion correction,
smoothing, filtering, or registration are

34
00:02:26,401 --> 00:02:27,884
not repeated unintentionally.

35
00:02:29,200 --> 00:02:33,823
The Data tab establishes the identity of
the model.

36
00:02:33,823 --> 00:02:38,446
It contains the four-dimensional
functional input, repetition time, number

37
00:02:38,446 --> 00:02:41,014
of volumes, and output directory.

38
00:02:41,014 --> 00:02:45,123
These values connect image sampling to
experimental timing.

39
00:02:45,123 --> 00:02:51,801
Later, we will verify them against the
image header and BIDS metadata before

40
00:02:51,801 --> 00:02:52,828
entering them.

41
00:02:52,828 --> 00:02:57,965
The Pre-stats tab controls preprocessing
operations such as motion correction,

42
00:02:57,965 --> 00:03:01,560
brain extraction, spatial smoothing, and
temporal filtering.

43
00:03:01,560 --> 00:03:03,615
These are scientific decisions.

44
00:03:03,615 --> 00:03:11,320
Applying a step twice is not neutral, and
leaving a required step off is not

45
00:03:11,320 --> 00:03:14,402
repaired by a plausible activation map.

46
00:03:14,402 --> 00:03:19,025
The Registration tab controls mappings
between functional, anatomical, and

47
00:03:19,025 --> 00:03:20,052
standard spaces.

48
00:03:20,052 --> 00:03:24,675
A completed transform only shows that an
optimisation finished.

49
00:03:24,675 --> 00:03:30,325
Registration quality must still be checked
visually across the brain, including

50
00:03:30,325 --> 00:03:34,435
cortical boundaries, ventricles,
cerebellum, and areas of incomplete

51
00:03:34,435 --> 00:03:35,462
functional coverage.

52
00:03:35,462 --> 00:03:39,571
The Stats tab defines the general linear
model.

53
00:03:39,571 --> 00:03:44,194
Here, explanatory variables represent task
conditions or nuisance structure.

54
00:03:44,194 --> 00:03:49,844
Task timing can be convolved with a
haemodynamic response, contrasts encode

55
00:03:49,844 --> 00:03:56,522
planned hypotheses, and the design preview
exposes the actual matrix FEAT will fit.

56
00:03:56,522 --> 00:04:01,658
Before running anything, the columns,
timing, correlations, and contrast weights

57
00:04:01,658 --> 00:04:06,281
must tell the same experimental story as
the protocol.

58
00:04:06,281 --> 00:04:10,391
The Post-stats tab controls thresholding
and result reporting.

59
00:04:10,391 --> 00:04:16,555
It is tempting to start with bright
clusters, but inference is only

60
00:04:16,555 --> 00:04:20,664
interpretable after the input,
preprocessing, registration, and design

61
00:04:20,664 --> 00:04:23,746
have passed their own quality-control
checks.

62
00:04:23,746 --> 00:04:28,369
The Misc tab contains auxiliary settings
and output options.

63
00:04:28,369 --> 00:04:36,587
Most projects use only a subset of them,
but they remain part of the saved design

64
00:04:36,587 --> 00:04:41,724
and should be reviewed when reproducing or
auditing an analysis.

65
00:04:45,533 --> 00:04:50,889
The practical order is Data, Pre-stats,
Registration, Stats, Post-stats, and then

66
00:04:50,889 --> 00:04:51,375
Misc.

67
00:04:51,375 --> 00:04:57,218
That order moves from the measured time
series, through preparation and spatial

68
00:04:57,218 --> 00:05:01,112
alignment, into the model and finally the
report.

69
00:05:01,112 --> 00:05:04,033
For now, leave the values unchanged.

70
00:05:04,033 --> 00:05:09,389
You have opened the intended FSL
environment, launched FEAT, selected a

71
00:05:09,389 --> 00:05:13,284
first-level scope, and identified what
each tab controls.

72
00:05:13,284 --> 00:05:21,073
In the next walkthrough, we will configure
the Data tab using a real BOLD run and

73
00:05:21,073 --> 00:05:24,481
verify every value against the source
files.
